{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WeHhoRvYJvsL1SB8YgKQoY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd111-ptx\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/ptx: Produce a Permuted Index\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS does not ship ptx. GNU ptx produces a permuted (keyword-in-context) index of\n6\t  text input. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gptx,\n7\t  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n8\t\n9\tgoals:\n10\t  - G1: Produce a permuted (KWIC) index from text input.\n11\t  - G2: Support output width, gap size, and reference control.\n12\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gptx via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: KWIC index generation\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must read input lines and produce a permuted index where each significant word appears as a keyword in context, with the surrounding text shown on either side.\n20\t\n21\t  R2:\n22\t    title: Index options\n23\t    items:\n24\t      - R2.1:\n25\t          text: \"-w N or --width=N must set the output line width (default 72). -g N or --gap-size=N must set the minimum gap between columns (default 3).\"\n26\t      - R2.2:\n27\t          text: \"-f or --ignore-case must fold lowercase to uppercase for sorting purposes.\"\n28\t      - R2.3:\n29\t          text: Must read from FILE or stdin when no file or \"-\" is given.\n30\t\n31\t  R3:\n32\t    title: Word regexp\n33\t    items:\n34\t      - R3.1:\n35\t          text: \"-W REGEXP or --word-regexp=REGEXP must use REGEXP to define what constitutes a word.\"\n36\t\n37\t  R4:\n38\t    title: Reference control\n39\t    items:\n40\t      - R4.1:\n41\t          text: \"-A or --auto-reference must produce automatically generated references based on file name and line number.\"\n42\t      - R4.2:\n43\t          text: \"-r or --references must treat the first field of each line as a reference and exclude it from the index.\"\n44\t\n45\t  R5:\n46\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n47\t    items:\n48\t      - R5.1:\n49\t          text: Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n50\t      - R5.2:\n51\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n52\t\n53\tnon_goals:\n54\t  - cmd/ptx does not implement TeX/roff output format in this release.\n55\t\n56\tacceptance_criteria:\n57\t  - id: AC1\n58\t    criterion: \"ptx on a text file produces a permuted index, matching gptx.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R1.1\n61\t      - R2.3\n62\t  - id: AC2\n63\t    criterion: \"ptx -f folds case for sorting, matching gptx -f.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R2.2\n66\t  - id: AC3\n67\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gptx passes.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t  - id: AC4\n71\t    criterion: \"cmd/ptx compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R2.1\n75\t      - R2.2\n76\t      - R2.3\n77\t      - R3.1\n78\t      - R4.1\n79\t      - R4.2\n80\t      - R5.1\n81\t      - R5.2\n82\t\n83\tpackage_contract:\n84\t  imports:\n85\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3596ca82-8fda-4731-9654-beb7f7457b9b","uuid":"438f660b-a921-48da-9676-1d1a5becdb80","timestamp":"2026-05-28T19:04:50.853Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5640/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd111-ptx.yaml","content":"id: srd111-ptx\ntitle: \"cmd/ptx: Produce a Permuted Index\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS does not ship ptx. GNU ptx produces a permuted (keyword-in-context) index of\n  text input. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gptx,\n  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Produce a permuted (KWIC) index from text input.\n  - G2: Support output width, gap size, and reference control.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gptx via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: KWIC index generation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must read input lines and produce a permuted index where each significant word appears as a keyword in context, with the surrounding text shown on either side.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Index options\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-w N or --width=N must set the output line width (default 72). -g N or --gap-size=N must set the minimum gap between columns (default 3).\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-f or --ignore-case must fold lowercase to uppercase for sorting purposes.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must read from FILE or stdin when no file or \"-\" is given.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Word regexp\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-W REGEXP or --word-regexp=REGEXP must use REGEXP to define what constitutes a word.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Reference control\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: \"-A or --auto-reference must produce automatically generated references based on file name and line number.\"\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"-r or --references must treat the first field of each line as a reference and exclude it from the index.\"\n\n  R5:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R5.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R5.2:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/ptx does not implement TeX/roff output format in this release.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"ptx on a text file produces a permuted index, matching gptx.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"ptx -f folds case for sorting, matching gptx -f.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gptx passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/ptx compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R5.1\n      - R5.2\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
